        "original_id": "a69bc682-7d60-531c-a2e8-1a82486496b8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams/Leagues: Houston Aeros, World Hockey Association, Detroit Red Wings, Hockey Hall of Fame\n- People: Gordie Howe, Sid Abel, Ted Lindsay\n- Topics: 1973–74 Houston Aeros season, Production Line\n\nFacts:\n- The 1973–74 Houston Aeros season was the Houston Aeros' second season of operation in the World Hockey Association.\n- The 1973–74 Houston Aeros season saw the debut of Gordie Howe and his sons in the World Hockey Association.\n- Gordie Howe was nicknamed \"Mr. Hockey\" and is considered one of the greatest ice hockey players of all time.\n- The Production Line of the Detroit Red Wings consisted of Gordie Howe at right wing, Sid Abel at centre, and Ted Lindsay at left wing.\n- Gordie Howe, Sid Abel, and Ted Lindsay were all members of the Hockey Hall of Fame.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
